# apix-x402-onramp — box .env template (the live cascade demo at demo.api-index.org)
#
# Copy to the box as /opt/onramp/.env (or ~/onramp/.env + export ONRAMP_ENV_FILE), fill the
# mnemonics, `chmod 600`. NEVER commit a filled copy. Mnemonics stay on the box only — the payTo
# ADDRESSES are public (like an IBAN) and already ship as defaults in application.yaml.
#
# ── WALLET MAP — read carefully: the onramp's INTERNAL names are INVERTED vs. the wallet names ──
#
#   Wallet name     Public address (IBAN-like)                                  Role in the cascade
#   ─────────────   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────  ───────────────────
#   AGENT           Q2XTPIACCO27OZ7ROPPT5SU5HLAZCELVGEGGSGRIMQBP5TBXHOHZWN6GOY   pays hop 1 (agent -> outer)
#   SERVICE A       GVRXJLXF6OJLRIV46CRIXLG3DX3RJYBBAGRKNNYLHWOAHG57GKWHDH6ZAE   OUTER service: receives from
#                                                                                AGENT, then PAYS hop 2
#   SERVICE B       EO63ZQECPU7IMHTSWOZKH7YBBS73PY72RJKCAMI3LHFT6LGMIR2W5ECIBE   INNER service: receives hop 2
#
#   Cascade:  AGENT --hop1 (0.03 USDC)--> SERVICE A --hop2 (0.01 USDC)--> SERVICE B
#
# The onramp calls the OUTER service "B" (route /gw/humanity) and the INNER service "A"
# (route /gw/sanctions-basic). So in env-var terms:
#   ONRAMP_B_* = the OUTER service = your SERVICE A
#   ONRAMP_A_* = the INNER service = your SERVICE B
# (Yes, it is crossed. The table above is the source of truth — match by ROLE, not by letter.)

# ── Secrets (mnemonics) — set on the box, never commit, never share (not even with the assistant) ──

# The INNER-hop payer: the OUTER service (your SERVICE A, GVRXJ…) paying the inner service over x402.
# BOOT-CRITICAL for the cascade — without it the second hop throws at call time.
ONRAMP_B_PAYER_MNEMONIC="<SERVICE A's 25 words>"

# The AGENT payer (your AGENT wallet, Q2XTP…): only needed if the server itself triggers hop 1
# (the server-side "Run the cascade" endpoint for jury self-check). Leave blank if the first hop is
# always driven by an external client that holds the agent wallet.
ONRAMP_PAYER_MNEMONIC="<AGENT's 25 words — optional, see above>"

# ── Public payTo addresses — OPTIONAL overrides (application.yaml already defaults to these) ──
# ONRAMP_A_PAYTO_ADDRESS = INNER receiver = your SERVICE B (EO63Z…)
# ONRAMP_B_PAYTO_ADDRESS = OUTER receiver = your SERVICE A (GVRXJ…)
#ONRAMP_A_PAYTO_ADDRESS="EO63ZQECPU7IMHTSWOZKH7YBBS73PY72RJKCAMI3LHFT6LGMIR2W5ECIBE"
#ONRAMP_B_PAYTO_ADDRESS="GVRXJLXF6OJLRIV46CRIXLG3DX3RJYBBAGRKNNYLHWOAHG57GKWHDH6ZAE"
